@node math-iir-fir User Guide
@section User Guide

End users do not call this crate. They see the result:

@itemize @bullet
@item The @code{eq} and @code{linear-phase-eq} plugins.
@item The crossover plugin (Linkwitz-Riley and linear-phase variants).
@item Filter exports in Equalizer APO, RME, AU Preset, CamillaDSP,
  EasyEffects, PipeWire, Roon and Wavelet formats.
@end itemize

@node math-iir-fir Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Generic precision

All filter types (@code{Biquad}, @code{SvfFilter}, @code{Fir},
@code{BiquadBank}) are generic over @code{FilterFloat} and default to
@code{f64}. Convenience aliases @code{BiquadF32}, @code{SvfFilterF32},
@dots{} exist when throughput matters more than precision.

@subheading Filter types

@table @asis
@item Biquad
@code{Peak}, @code{Lowpass}, @code{Highpass}, @code{Lowshelf},
@code{Highshelf}, @code{Bandpass}, @code{Notch}, @code{AllPass}.
@item SVF (state-variable filter)
Zero-delay-feedback topology (Zavalishin TPT) for artefact-free
parameter changes.
@item FIR
Windowed sinc bank for linear-phase filtering, FIR design from
frequency response, Kirkeby correction, pre-ringing suppression.
@item Crossovers
Linkwitz-Riley 4th-order IIR and linear-phase FIR.
@end table

@subheading Offline analysis

@code{filtfilt} and @code{sosfilt} provide zero-phase filtering for
analysis tasks (e.g.@: in @code{math-rir}).

@subheading PEQ

The @code{ParametricEQ} type owns a list of biquads plus a preamp. It
can compute SPL response, apply loudness compensation, and export to
the nine formats above.

@subheading Testing

@example
cargo test -p math-iir-fir
@end example

Biquad benchmarks live in @file{benches/}; run with
@code{cargo bench -p math-iir-fir}.
